tangular or curved) at the street edge; older ramps are plain or grooved concrete with no domes\u2014detect both. Count a curb ramp wherever the curb visibly drops to street level at a pedestrian crossing point, even if it is old, cracked, steep, narrow, missing detectable warnings, partly hidden, or far away. Box the full ramp structure (sloped run, flares, and warning surface) from where it leaves sidewalk level down to the gutter. A parallel ramp or a blended transition gets one box. If a corner has two ramps separated by raised curb or grass, box each; a single apex ramp serving both crossings gets one box. Exclude driveway and alley aprons (vehicle curb cuts, usually wider and mid-block, leading to garages, alleys, or parking, with no domes and the sidewalk staying level across them), full-height curbs with no lowered section, and storm drain inlets. Return one tight bounding box per curb ramp. Do not box driveways, stairs, or crosswalk paint. If there are no curb ramps, return an empty list. For each box, also give a score from 0 to 100 for how confident you are that it is a curb ramp. Use the whole range: 50 means you are unsure.","provider":"gemini","response_schema":"{\"items\": {\"properties\": {\"box_2d\": {\"description\": \"[ymin, xmin, ymax, xmax], normalized 0-1000\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"label\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"score\": {\"maximum\": 100, \"minimum\": 0, \"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"propertyOrdering\": [\"box_2d\", \"label\", \"score\"], \"required\": [\"box_2d\", \"label\", \"score\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}","source_max_edge":4096,"tile":true,"views":[[0.0,-30.0,90.0,90.0,1024,1024],[60.0,-30.0,90.0,90.0,1024,1024],[120.0,-30.0,90.0,90.0,1024,1024],[180.0,-30.0,90.0,90.0,1024,1024],[240.0,-30.0,90.0,90.0,1024,1024],[300.0,-30.0,90.0,90.0,1024,1024]]}}